{
  "name": "What to Do When Your Rental Property Needs a Repair",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When a repair pops up at your rental property, it can feel like a headache, right? But with a good system, you can handle things smoothly. First, figure out if it’s urgent. A leaky faucet isn’t usually an emergency, but a burst pipe definitely is! Document everything, from the tenant’s report to photos of the issue. Sometimes, you might need a temporary fix while you get the full repair sorted. Next, you’ll want to get some cost estimates. For bigger jobs, especially anything involving plumbing, electrical, or HVAC, always make sure the tradespeople are licensed and insured. Abraham and his team at HH Remodeling LLC can help with a lot of these interior fixes, like drywall, tile, and even general handyman services, and they can coordinate with plumbers and electricians for the specialized stuff. Once the work is done, confirm everything’s fixed with before-and-after photos. It’s all about clear communication with your tenants and the contractors to keep everyone happy and your property in good shape. Need help with a repair? Give HH Remodeling LLC a call at 303-505-0866; they serve the greater Denver area.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
